{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe layered defenses against the attestation-laundering anti-pattern — tagging a CODE-VERIFIABLE acceptance criterion `[operator-attested]` so the completion verifier accepts a ticket comment instead of repository proof — failed to reject a live instance.\n\n## Reproduction (today, epic fb8a-7363-e406-4e36 close)\n1. Epic close failed: completion verifier hit its step budget (request_limit=24) and reported AC-19 unmet — though its proof is repo-resident (tests/unit/test_scan_scoping.py::test_fsck_default_skips_archived_and_flag_restores et al., merged 39de64871c).\n2. The operator retagged AC-19 `[operator-attested]` (the anti-pattern; a misclassification — the evidence is an exact path/symbol repository fact).\n3. `rebar review-plan fb8a-7363-e406-4e36` → PASS. Expected: the evidence-kind criterion (criteria_routing.json \"FIRE on … a tagged repository fact grounded by exact path/symbol evidence\") fires; also the AC carried NO `provenance:` continuation line, which det_measurement_provenance (plan_review/det_measurement_provenance.py) is supposed to require on every tagged AC.\n4. Close succeeded: the completion verifier accepted the tag at face value — correct per its prompt (completion_verifier.md \"How you classify a criterion: SOLELY from an author tag\"; ADR-0043 makes the tag a trust escape hatch), which is exactly why the REVIEW-side guards must be the rejection point.\n\n## Suspected defects (investigate all)\n- Evidence-kind criterion did not fire on a tagged repo-provable AC at re-review time (routing overlay not applied? criterion advisory instead of blocking? re-review of an in_progress ticket skips it?).\n- det_measurement_provenance did not flag the missing `provenance:` line (same questions; det_floor.py wiring says ADVISORY — if so, advisory is insufficient for this class).\n- Consider a deterministic pre-close guard: a criterion whose text cites an exact repo path/symbol (or whose evidence comment does) but carries the tag is auto-rejected before any LLM runs.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Root cause identified for why the plan-review evidence-kind guard passed a tagged repository fact (with the failing review run cited).\n- [x] A mistagged code-verifiable AC (repo path/symbol evidence exists) is REJECTED before close: reproduced RED with a fixture ticket, then GREEN after the fix.\n- [x] A tagged AC missing its `provenance:` continuation line is rejected (or the advisory is promoted to blocking for close-path reviews), with tests.\n- [x] Legitimately external ACs (deploy/vote/console evidence with provenance) still pass: guard test.\n- [x] [operator-attested] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786751285986088001,"uuid":"013798ce-4c87-48de-923a-bf6b7c35860a"}